Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 05:26:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Phase 5 slice 5A: runway anchors are not dense fan-out
 stubs

The first 27-cell table with PHOTONIC_ROUTER_PORT_RUNWAYS=1 (b05bffd) lost
six cells on crossing legality and ADEPT 32x32 lidar-pure gained two
crossings: the runway anchors had entered every consumer of
fanout_anchor_by_port_spec, including the ones that carry the dense
fan-out semantics, so each runway port's access footprint shrank to the
stub lane size 0 (siblings cut in right in front of the ports), its ports
formed a dense cluster, its nets were exempt from the long-straight
penalty, the dense target reservations skipped it and the footprint was
laid from the anchor.

SessionState.fanout_stub_anchor hides runway anchors from those consumers
(_resolve_port_footprint_cells, the port-opening centre, the dense lateral
windows, _dense_target_port_runway_lengths, the static stub clusters,
apply_long_straight_fanout_exemption via the new fanout_stub_net_ids, the
topological-stub order). The geometry consumers (search endpoints, stub
prepend, static cells, endpoint correction) still take every anchor.

Switch off: nine-cell gate exact, 712 Python tests. Switch on: nine cells
keep their crossings and 0 errors, Benes lidar-pure lengths +1.0/+1.1 %
(were +0.5 % with the collapsed footprints), the other cells unchanged to
+0.7 %; Benes 16x16 lidar-pure routes again with 88 crossings. Regression
test in tests/test_port_runways.py.

